+++ b/board/freescale/gateway_dk/README
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+Mono Gateway Development Kit
+============================
+
+The Gateway Development Kit (Gateway-DK) is Mono's LS1046A-based
+network appliance development platform.
+
+ - NXP QorIQ LS1046A, 4x Cortex-A72
+ - 8 GB DDR4 at 2100 MT/s with ECC, soldered down (static
+   controller init in TF-A, no SPD)
+ - 3x 1 Gbit/s copper ports (SGMII, MaxLinear GPY115 PHYs)
+ - 2x 10 Gbit/s SFP+ cages (XFI, DS100DF410 retimer)
+ - 64 MB QSPI NOR flash (Micron MT25QU512ABB) and eMMC
+ - USB Type-C (HD3SS3220 controller, STUSB4500 USB-PD)
+ - Board management on I2C: PCA9545 muxes at 0x70, AT24CS32
+   board-info EEPROM, PCF2131 RTC, EMC2302 fan controller, TMP431
+   temperature sensors, INA234 rail monitors, 6V49205B clock
+   generator, LP58xx status LED controller
+
+SerDes configuration (RCW protocol 0x1133_0x5A06)
+-------------------------------------------------
+SerDes1: XFI.9, XFI.10 (SFP+ cages), SGMII.5, SGMII.6
+SerDes2: PCIe1 x1, SGMII.2, unused, PCIe3 x1
+
+Ethernet MACs map to physical ports left to right:
+fm1-mac5, fm1-mac6, fm1-mac2 (1G), fm1-mac9, fm1-mac10 (10G).
+Model, serial number and per-port MAC addresses are read from the
+board-info EEPROM into the environment at boot; the program_eeprom
+command provisions them at the factory.
+
+Boot flow
+---------
+The board boots through TF-A (TFABOOT). The SoC loads BL2 from QSPI
+or eMMC as selected by a DIP switch, BL2 loads the FIP (BL31 plus
+U-Boot as BL33), and U-Boot runs the per-component hardware
+self-test from misc_init_r() before booting Linux. The self-test
+verdict is surfaced on the status LED and passed to the kernel via
+the bootargs_hwtest environment variable.
+
+Firmware layout (32 MB image)
+-----------------------------
+Offset      Size   Content
+0x00000000  1 MB   RCW + PBI + BL2
+0x00100000  2 MB   FIP (BL31 + U-Boot)
+0x00300000  1 MB   U-Boot environment (8 KB used)
+0x00400000  1 MB   FMan microcode
+0x00500000  1 MB   Recovery device tree
+0x00600000  4 MB   Unallocated
+0x00A00000 22 MB   Recovery kernel + initramfs
+
+The eMMC layout is identical except that BL2 is written at a 4 KB
+offset (the boot ROM fetches it from there), which keeps the
+partition table sector intact.
+
+Building
+--------
+U-Boot alone:
+
+    make mono_gateway_dk_defconfig
+    make
+
+Complete firmware images are assembled by the meta-mono Yocto layer:
+https://github.com/we-are-mono/meta-mono
